{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"effete-barbaric-xiaosaurus","creation_channel":"cli","description":"# Ratchet `Any` and loose typing repo-wide\n\n**Filed for later — deliberately OUTSIDE epic e369 and out of scope for the session that discovered\nit.** Not decomposed yet; needs planning before execution.\n\n## Drivers\n\n1. **Navigability.** Serena/Pyright resolve references only through TYPED receivers. An `Any` makes\n   the LSP return a FALSE EMPTY — not an error — so `find_referencing_symbols` reports a symbol as\n   unused when it has real call sites. See [rebar:dbf9-3fc8-625d-4730].\n2. **Contracts between components, hence testability and reliability.** A port typed as `Any` cannot\n   be enforced, so a component can silently fail to satisfy the interface it claims. See\n   [rebar:cc77-8120-bcc6-47e8] and its root-caused defect [rebar:a357-b747-ece9-4cf5].\n\n## Measured baseline (AST scan of `src/rebar`, this repo, today)\n\n    TOTAL defs = 3271     untyped defs = 351     Any-annotated params/returns = 1192\n\n    package          defs  untyped  Any-ann\n    llm              1094      122      544\n    _engine           701      109      387\n    grounding         149        0      103\n    _commands         295       61       12\n    <top-level>       320       38       25\n    metrics            84        0       57\n    review_bot         66        1       15\n\n**The loose-typing surface is ~3.4x the untyped surface** (1192 vs 351). Any effort aimed only at\n'annotate the unannotated' addresses the smaller half.\n\n## The finding that motivates this story\n\nrebar already has a documented, enforced, shrink-only **mypy strictness ratchet**\n(`pyproject.toml`, per-package `disallow_untyped_defs`, guarded by `test_mypy_ratchet.py`).\nCurrently enabled: `rebar.graph.*` and `rebar.grounding.*`.\n\n**`grounding` passed that ratchet with 0 untyped defs and 103 `Any` annotations.** So a package can\nsatisfy the existing gate while remaining opaque to both the type checker and the LSP. The ratchet\nmeasures the wrong thing for these two drivers — it is necessary but not sufficient.\n\nProven directly (mypy, repo settings):\n\n    def f(client, ...):                  client.set_entity_property(...)   -> NO ERROR\n    def f(client: Any, ...):             client.set_entity_property(...)   -> NO ERROR   <-- passes the ratchet\n    def f(client: TicketTransport, ...): client.set_entity_property(...)\n        -> error: \"TicketTransport\" has no attribute \"set_entity_property\"  [attr-defined]\n\nOnly the third line buys either driver.\n\n## Approach sketch (needs planning, not yet a plan)\n\n* Distinguish LEGITIMATE `Any` from LAZY `Any`. Some are unavoidable — genuine dynamic boundaries\n  (JSON payloads, `spec_from_file_location` loaders, third-party stubs). The story is NOT 'delete\n  every Any'; it is 'every remaining Any is deliberate and justified'. A blanket ban would be worse\n  than the status quo because it invites `cast()` noise that hides the same blindness.\n* Prioritise by DRIVER, not by count: an `Any` on a PORT/interface boundary (the transport, the\n  Backend roles, the LLM runner seam) is worth many in a leaf helper. `_engine` and `llm` carry the\n  most, but the ranking that matters is 'is this a contract between components'.\n* Extend the existing ratchet rather than inventing a parallel mechanism — e.g. add a per-package\n  `disallow_any_explicit` (or an Any-count budget) with the same shrink-only enforcement and the\n  same `test_mypy_ratchet.py` guard, so packages are promoted deliberately and cannot regress.\n* Consider a targeted first slice to prove the shape (the reconciler transport surface is already\n  scoped by [rebar:cc77-8120-bcc6-47e8]) before attempting `llm` at 544.\n\n## Acceptance criteria (provisional — refine at planning time)\n\n- [ ] a documented distinction between justified and unjustified `Any`, with the justified ones\n      annotated or otherwise marked so they are not re-litigated\n- [ ] the ratchet is extended to constrain `Any` (not only unannotated defs), shrink-only, enforced\n      by the existing ratchet test\n- [ ] `docs/architecture.md`'s ratchet section records that `disallow_untyped_defs` is satisfied by\n      `Any` and therefore does not by itself deliver either driver\n- [ ] at least one component boundary is converted end-to-end as the worked example, with evidence\n      that Serena reference-finding works across it afterwards (the navigability driver, measured —\n      not assumed)\n- [ ] a measured before/after on the counts above, so the ratchet has a baseline to shrink from","id":"06e0-fb68-657a-4ea1","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"story","title":"Ratchet Any and loose typing repo-wide: typed contracts for navigability and testability"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1785479760721669001,"uuid":"ba977e23-d35a-489f-a9b2-f11682097dd8"}